{
  "_id": "Fw6Yl3arxhCvmBFZ",
  "name": "Grasping Reach",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/skills/melee/strike-polearm-glowing-white.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<blockquote><p><em>Your reach extends considerably past where your reach ought to end. Enemies who thought themselves safely spaced find themselves seized, dragged, and repositioned, and objects on the far side of a room are no longer meaningfully on the far side of anything.</em></p></blockquote>\n<p><strong>1st Level</strong></p><ul><li>Your melee unarmed Strikes and melee weapons you wield gain the reach trait, or increase their reach by 5 feet if they already have it.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>5th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Your reach increases by another 5 feet.</li><li>You may Interact with objects anywhere within your reach.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>10th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Once per round, when you hit a creature within your reach, you may move it up to 10 feet in any direction as a free action.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>15th Level</strong></p><ul><li>Your reach increases by another 5 feet.</li><li>The forced movement increases to 15 feet.</li><li>Once per round, you may Grab, Shove, Trip, or Disarm a creature within your reach as a free action.</li></ul>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>In Foundry:</strong> your reach is raised automatically: 5 feet at 1st, 10 at 5th, 15 at 15th, on top of any reach a weapon already has.</p>\n<p>For the table: Interacting at reach, the forced movement on a hit from 10th (a note on your melee hits reminds you), and the free maneuver from 15th.</p>",
      "gm": ""
    },
